# Little Browser: each window remembers its space across restarts (chromium/lb sidebar). The
# space id is saved as window extra data — like Chromium's own vertical-tab collapsed state — and
# a restored window is put back on its space before its tabs come back.
# Restoring into an existing window (the crash bubble's Restore) moves that window to the saved
# window's space too. A window reopened through tab restore (only extensions do that here, with
# chrome.sessions.restore) goes back to its space the same way.

